    "voiceover": {
      "text": "Step Three: This is very important. Bend your knees, NOT your back! Keep your spine straight and aligned. Your knees and hips should do the work of lowering your body to the level of the bucket. Your back is not designed to bend when lifting heavy loads. A straight back protects your spine from serious injury. Always remember: bend your knees and keep your back straight.",
