      "text": "Step Six: Setting Down Properly. This is just as important as lifting. Approach your storage location or cleaning station, position your feet correctly, and reverse the lifting process. Bend at your knees and hips, keeping your back straight. Lower the bucket slowly and carefully. Never drop or throw the bucket, no matter how tired you are. A safe set-down completes a safe lift and protects your back.",
